WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.396
Homecare now brings market research and product development into one workspace.

00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:11.633
This guide covers the current website: browsing products, comparing national brands, and building a white-label proposal.

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.766
Start with the main navigation.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:21.473
Browse competitors, Global retailers and items, Sales and analysis, and White Label Workshop are the main working sections.

00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:24.456
Brands and factories and Video guide are resources.

00:00:24.636 --> 00:00:26.303
Opportunities comes last.

00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:30.754
To find international products, open Global retailers and items.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:35.379
Choose a Country or market, then a Retailer, and use Find an item to search.

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:38.359
For China, use the China listings shortcut.

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:41.492
Open Source listing to check the retailer's own page.

00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:46.622
Use Select to compare on a global product card, or Select in the original catalog.

00:00:46.802 --> 00:00:48.903
Compare selected opens your shortlist.

00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:53.004
Export selected CSV downloads the selected records for Excel.

00:00:53.184 --> 00:00:57.071
Product photos are exported as links, rather than embedded pictures.

00:00:57.471 --> 00:01:00.051
Sales and analysis shows the saved evidence.

00:01:00.231 --> 00:01:06.292
Compare sales figures only when the retailer, metric, reporting period, and snapshot date match.

00:01:06.472 --> 00:01:08.751
Missing sales information stays unknown.

00:01:08.931 --> 00:01:11.098
Research coverage is not market share.

00:01:11.498 --> 00:01:14.832
White Label Workshop opens a dedicated workshop page.

00:01:15.012 --> 00:01:17.971
Choose a Home-care subcategory and a Product concept.

00:01:18.151 --> 00:01:22.885
Explore laundry, storage, waste, odor control, and accessories.

00:01:23.065 --> 00:01:29.034
Follow the three review steps: Real products, Why and what changes, then Design and costs.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:31.874
Start with National-brand photo references.

00:01:32.054 --> 00:01:35.154
The laundry sorter uses Joseph Joseph and Brabantia.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.072
Choose View full-size photo to inspect the image.

00:01:38.252 --> 00:01:44.529
Read its match note, Size and capacity, Manufacturer data, and Photo source before comparing.

00:01:44.929 --> 00:01:47.258
Next, open Why and what changes.

00:01:47.438 --> 00:01:51.566
Read Why consider white label, then expand Brand reference and proof needed.

00:01:51.746 --> 00:01:57.508
Suggested changes also compares existing features, proposed improvements, and validation.

00:01:57.688 --> 00:02:00.298
These ideas still need a Target assortment check.

00:02:00.698 --> 00:02:04.100
Continue to Design and costs for the proposed Blender concept.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.732
Use Specs and dimensions to switch between millimetres and inches.

00:02:07.912 --> 00:02:10.441
Choose a finish to update the interactive model.

00:02:10.621 --> 00:02:13.156
Use Studio, Front, or Exploded.

00:02:13.336 --> 00:02:16.819
The rebuilt laundry sorter also has Inside and Details views.

00:02:17.219 --> 00:02:20.800
BOM and pricing lets you adjust component costs and assumptions.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:24.018
Enter a duty rate before calculating landed cost.

00:02:24.198 --> 00:02:28.958
Costs and proposed retail prices are planning estimates, not supplier quotes.

00:02:29.358 --> 00:02:36.425
Download the Blender development pack for the base Sage model, renders, dimensions, specifications, and BOM.

00:02:36.605 --> 00:02:42.296
Save brief with comparison photos keeps your selected finish and pricing edits in an HTML brief.

00:02:42.476 --> 00:02:45.979
Export references and changes saves a source-linked CSV.

00:02:46.159 --> 00:02:48.256
Review Validation before proceeding.

00:02:48.656 --> 00:02:53.920
Use Opportunities last to investigate possible gaps after reviewing the products and evidence.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.670
Music and button sounds have separate controls.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.987
You can keep the workspace quiet while you browse, compare, and develop.
